Turnip 26.2.0: the chip ids of the Adreno 850, 845, 753 and a second 735.

Turnip refuses a GPU whose chip id is not in its device table
(VK_ERROR_INCOMPATIBLE_DRIVER); DXVK then gets no Vulkan instance and the game
cannot start. Turnip 26.2.0 lacks four ids of Android GPUs:

  0x44051431  Adreno 850  Mesa merge request 45384 by Qualcomm, "freedreno: add
  0x44041430  Adreno 845  basic device support for Adreno 850 and 845" (open on
                          13 Nov 2026, commit c3b3ef956b896fe3c58f6991890c9ffd08fd6baa)
  0x43030e01  Adreno 735  Mesa 26.3.0, in the group of FD735 (same device info)
  0x43051701  Adreno 753  Mesa 26.3.0, in the group of FD750 (same device info)

The app ships the prebuilt usr/lib/libvulkan_freedreno.so of the turnip-26.2.0
package of Winlator 11.2 (window system integration of its own, source not
published), so the driver is not rebuilt. Records of GPUs that no Android
device has take the new ids: the Adreno X2-85 and X1-85 (laptop parts of the
Snapdragon X Elite / X2 Elite), the X1-45 (laptop) and the Adreno 200 (record
0, a generation Turnip does not drive). Mesa uses the first record that
matches; an id can match more than one (exact and fallback records), so the
order was checked: every id that matched a kept record before still matches it.

- 850 and 845 share one device info, the 840's with six more raw magic
  registers (RB_BIN_FOVEAT_XY_FDM_OFFSET 0..5 = 0, registers 0x8960..0x8965).
  The X2-85's info (__info35) differs from the 840's only in
  shading_rate_matches_vk and has 22 of 64 magic_raw slots in use; it gets
  that flag and the six registers in slots 22..27. The merge request's second
  commit also sets has_fdm_offset_gmem_clamping_disable, a field 26.2.0 does
  not have; it only matters with VK_QCOM_fragment_density_map_offset.
- 735 (0x43030e01): the X1-45's record already points to FD735's info; it gets
  the id and FD735's name.
- 753 (0x43051701): record 0 gets the id, gpu_id 0, and FD750's name and info.
- The names "Adreno (TM) 850" and "Adreno (TM) 845" are written over the
  strings "Adreno (TM) X2-85" (used by record 83 only) and "Adreno (TM) X2-90"
  (unused since turnip-a840v2).

